From 89d37cbc0a451e1835a214bbbb97f0f497b5583f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:03:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban-sync): an idle sync round skips the no-op apply,
 unchanged repair scans and per-poll connection opens [daveey]

Gateway profile 2026-10-31 (example-investigation, SIGUSR2 Python frames + native sample): the Board sync loop was
the largest idle consumer in the Desktop gateway's executor (~10% of a core):
- pull() ran apply_remote_changes on every empty feed page, a write transaction rewriting applying/cursor to the
  same values on every board every 5 s round;
- repair_partition_links toggled applying whenever a foreign edge to a card outside this file existed (forever);
- the pure repair scans (partition links, remote parents, divergence, missing children, lost placeholder links)
  re-read both files every round: ~330 ms CPU per round on the MacBook's default board;
- outbox_pending opened a fresh connection (schema re-parse) per board every 0.5 s: ~13 ms per pass.

Now an empty page with an unmoved cursor and applying=0 returns without a transaction; partition repair toggles
applying only for edges it will insert; sync_board skips the repair scans when their inputs are unchanged (live
file PRAGMA data_version on a kept read connection, replica inode+cursor, mode, gateway, placement config), read
before the scans so any commit during or after them re-arms the next round; outbox_pending reuses one kept
read-only connection per board file, reopened when the file is replaced. No TTL: every skip is keyed on state.
